6. GPU bottleneck mental model

Always split GPU problems into four buckets:

1. Compute-bound
   Tensor cores/SMs saturated

2. Memory-bandwidth-bound
   HBM reads/writes dominate

3. Capacity-bound
   GPU memory full / OOM / fragmentation

4. Launch/scheduling-bound
   many small kernels and CPU gaps
Tools
nvidia-smi: first glance only
DCGM exporter: production GPU metrics
Nsight Systems: timeline, gaps, memcopies, launch behavior
Nsight Compute: kernel-level compute vs memory analysis
Fixes
Compute-bound:
  FP16/BF16/FP8
  TensorRT-LLM
  better batch size
  tensor parallelism

Memory-bandwidth-bound:
  quantization
  KV-cache quantization
  FlashAttention/PagedAttention
  reduce context length
  better cache locality

Capacity-bound:
  reduce max sequence length
  reduce batch size
  lower max_num_seqs
  model sharding
  MIG/dedicated GPU
  quantization

Launch-bound:
  CUDA Graphs
  operator fusion
  TensorRT
  larger batches
  reduce small kernels

Strong answer:

“I do not ask only whether GPU utilization is high. I ask whether we are compute-bound, HBM-bandwidth-bound, memory-capacity-bound, or launch-bound.”

